### SAFE-MIN-001: prior_restore_evidence_present uses CWD-relative git commands

Lines 452-453: `git diff HEAD -- "$log_path"` and `git log -p -- "$log_path"` have no -C flag. If operator runs from a different working directory, the call silently returns false → Gate 3 silently bypassed.

Fix: derive REPO_ROOT from the script path at script top:
```bash
REPO_ROOT="$(cd "$(dirname "$(readlink -f "$0" 2>/dev/null || echo "$0")")/.." && pwd)"
```
(readlink -f compatibility note: macOS readlink doesn't support -f without coreutils; fallback to `$0` preserves existing behaviour when readlink -f fails).

Use `git -C "$REPO_ROOT" diff/log` in prior_restore_evidence_present.

