{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,260p' policies/VERSIONING.md\"","aggregated_output":"# SCP Federation Primitive — Versioning Contract\n\n**Status:** active as of slice 020H.1 (2026-05-01).\n**Closes:** WP-SCP-020 §4 020H.1 sub-criteria (i) + (ii).\n\n---\n\n## Scope\n\nThis document defines the semver contract that the SCP federation\nprimitive guarantees to adopters who pin a `# tag: v<X>.<Y>.<Z>`\nwrapper at `.github/workflows/policy-check.yml`. It covers three\npublic surfaces:\n\n1. **Reusable workflow inputs** — `workflow_call.inputs` declared on\n   `.github/workflows/policy-check.yml`.\n2. **Schema contracts** — JSON Schema at\n   `schemas/policy-check-summary.schema.json` (the structured\n   summary artefact every adopter consumes for nightly + release-gate\n   reconciliation), `schemas/rule-config.schema.json`, and\n   `schemas/scorecard-emit.schema.json` (the opt-in cross-repo\n   scorecard emit per WP-SCP-023 023B / D-041 — added at v1.2.0;\n   MAJOR-pinned per WP-SCP-023 plan-doc §10 Q1).\n3. **Rule IDs** — the `SCP-R-NNN` identifiers under `policies/`.\n4. **Opt-in workflow inputs** — `scorecard-emit: bool` (added at\n   v1.2.0 per WP-SCP-023 023B; default false). Opt-in inputs follow\n   the same MINOR/MAJOR semver category as core inputs.\n\nIt does NOT cover internal-only surfaces: `lib/policy_check_invocation.sh`,\n`scripts/scp-policy-check.lock`, helper scripts in `scripts/`, the\nRenovate preset internal shape, the OPA Rego `scp_common.rego`\nhelpers, or the SCP-self cross-repo aggregator pipeline\n(`.github/workflows/scorecard-aggregator.yml`,\n`schemas/scorecard-opt-in-registry.schema.json`,\n`schemas/scorecard-index.schema.json`,\n`docs/scorecards/opt-in-registry.yaml`,\n`output/scorecards/index.json` — added in slice 023C / D-042; mirrors\n`.github/workflows/conflict-gate.yml` posture per slice 020N).\nThese are refactored without notice.\n\n---\n\n## Semver guarantee\n\n**`MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH`** with strict semantic-versioning meaning:\n\n| Bump | When | Adopter action required |\n|---|---|---|\n| **PATCH** (`v1.0.x`) | Bug fixes, new informational annotations, performance improvements, observability records, internal refactors of helpers/lib. | None — drop in the SHA bump and merge. |\n| **MINOR** (`v1.x.0`) | New `workflow_call` inputs (with safe defaults), new `SCP-R-NNN` rules added with `threshold: warn` baseline, new optional schema fields, new commit-status contexts (informational), new `disabled_rules:` reasons. | Recommended: review the release notes for new rules. None mandatory unless the adopter wants to opt into a new rule's `threshold: deny`. |\n| **MAJOR** (`vX.0.0`) | Breaking changes — see \"What is breaking\" below. | **Mandatory** — read the migration guide in the release notes; an amending decision row in adopter's `DECISIONS.md` (or equivalent) before bumping the SHA pin. |\n\n---\n\n## What counts as a breaking change\n\nAny of the following requires a MAJOR bump and an amending decision row:\n\n### Workflow inputs\n\n- Removing a `workflow_call.inputs.<name>`.\n- Renaming a `workflow_call.inputs.<name>`.\n- Changing the `default:` value of an input in a way that flips an existing adopter's effective behaviour (e.g. `threshold: warn` → `threshold: deny`).\n- Changing the `type:` of an input.\n- Making a previously-optional input required.\n\n### Schema contracts\n\n- Removing a previously-required field from `policy-check-summary.schema.json` or `rule-config.schema.json`.\n- Renaming any field (use add-new-then-deprecate instead).\n- Tightening a string `pattern:` such that previously-valid values are rejected.\n- Tightening a `format:` constraint (e.g. `date` → `date-time`).\n- Adding a new required field (covered by the deprecation ramp — see below).\n- Removing an `enum:` value that was previously emitted.\n\n### Rule IDs\n\n- Removing an `SCP-R-NNN` rule.\n- Re-numbering an `SCP-R-NNN` rule (the ID is the durable contract; the underlying logic is internal).\n- Promoting a rule from `threshold: warn` to `threshold: deny` as the **default** at the SCP source. (Adopters may always override per-rule via `.scp/rule-config.yaml`; the default flip is what's breaking.)\n- Tightening a rule's match scope such that previously-passing manifests now deny.\n\n### Read-back / annotation contracts\n\n- Removing `scp/policy-check-readback` commit-status posting.\n- Removing a `::warning::` or `::error::` annotation surface that adopters' downstream tooling parses (e.g. an annotation parser that grouped on `title=SCP-E001`).\n- Renaming an `SCP-ENNN` error-code identifier.\n\n### Branch-protection helper\n\n- Removing `--repo`, `--branch`, `--plan`, `--no-enforce-admins`, `--i-understand-this-bypasses-the-gate`, `--restore`, `--expected-wrapper-sha`, `--i-understand-restore-removes-admin-enforcement`, `--i-understand-restore-removes-required-checks`, `--i-understand-this-repo-has-no-prior-green-ci`, or `--i-understand-no-gate-2-verification` flags from `scripts/enable-required-check.sh`.\n- Changing the script's invocation-log markdown block schema.\n\n### Tag protection\n\n- Changing the `v*` or `renovate/v*` Repository Ruleset shape (deletion / non-fast-forward / update behaviour).\n\n---\n\n## What does NOT count as breaking\n\n- Adding new `workflow_call.inputs.<name>` with a safe default.\n- Adding new `SCP-R-NNN` rules at `threshold: warn` baseline.\n- Adding new schema fields (`additionalProperties: false` is preserved — but new fields are added under existing properties, not as required new top-level fields).\n- Adding new `enum:` values that were not previously emitted.\n- Adding new `disabled_rules:` reasons.\n- Adding new informational `::warning::` or `::error::` titles (if existing titles preserved).\n- Internal helper-library refactors.\n- New commit-status contexts (the existing two are stable).\n- New OPA / Conftest / Regal binary version bumps in the lockfile (these are SHA-pinned; adopters get the new pins via Renovate auto-bump).\n\n---\n\n## Deprecation ramp (one-release warning window)\n\n**Closes 020H.1 sub-criterion (ii); enforced by 020H.3 release-gate.**\n\nWhen the SCP source needs to remove or breaking-change one of the\npublic surfaces above, the change MUST proceed via a **one-release\ndeprecation ramp**:\n\n1. **Release N: add the new surface** (alongside the old surface), and\n   in the same release add a `::warning::` annotation to the old\n   surface stating: `<surface> deprecated; use <new-surface>; will be\n   removed in v<X+1>.0.0`. Document in release notes. **Add an entry\n   to `policies/deprecations.yaml`** with `announced_at`,\n   `announced_release`, `target_release`, and `migration_pointer`\n   (per `schemas/deprecations.schema.json`).\n2. **Release N+1 (the next MINOR or MAJOR — whichever lands first):**\n   keep both surfaces live; the warning continues to fire.\n3. **Release N+M (the MAJOR after the next MINOR):** old surface is\n   removed; the MAJOR bump is the breaking-change vehicle. An amending\n   decision row in `docs/DECISIONS.md` records the removal. **Remove\n   the entry from `policies/deprecations.yaml`** as part of the\n   removal commit.\n\nThe minimum gap between deprecation announcement (step 1) and\nremoval (step 3) is **one MINOR release**. Adopters who track every\nMINOR release see at least one full PR cycle's worth of warnings\nbefore the surface vanishes.\n\n**Machine enforcement** — two operating modes per `.github/workflows/release-gate.yml`:\n\n1. **Dry-run pre-flight (workflow_dispatch).** The pre-emptive\n   enforcement path. The operator runs the gate BEFORE pushing the\n   tag:\n\n   ```bash\n   gh workflow run release-gate.yml -f dry_run_tag=v1.1.0\n   # Wait for the run to start, then watch for completion + non-zero\n   # exit on failure (gh run list always exits 0; gh run watch with\n   # --exit-status surfaces the workflow's verdict). Closes 020H.3 R2\n   # nit-SAFE-001.\n   sleep 5  # allow the dispatch to register\n   RUN_ID=\"$(gh run list --workflow=release-gate.yml --limit 1 --json databaseId --jq '.[0].databaseId')\"\n   gh run watch \"${RUN_ID}\" --exit-status\n   ```\n\n   If the dry-run exits clean, the tag is safe to push. **The\n   dry-run pre-flight is mandatory before every v* tag-cut.**\n\n2. **Post-tag observer (`push: tags: ['v*']`).** GitHub Actions\n   cannot block a `push: tags` event — by the time the workflow\n   fires, the tag already exists on the remote. This trigger\n   therefore acts as a last-line-of-defense observer: it annotates\n   the bad tag with `SCP-EREL-001` AND opens a\n   `release-gate-violation` GitHub issue auto-assigned to `@jrnb2024`\n   for triage (per slice 020H.3.1 closure of TF-020H3rg-003 —\n   `permissions: { issues: write }` on the workflow + de-dup by tag,\n   matching the canary-replay.yml pattern). The bad tag itself is\n   immutable per D-030 (the `scp-tag-protection-v` Repository\n   Ruleset blocks deletion + force-push + non-fast-forward, including\n   for admins).\n\nBoth modes evaluate the same TWO invariants:\n\n- any `policies/deprecations.yaml` entry has `target_release` matching\n  the candidate tag AND `announced_release` is not at least one MINOR\n  behind the candidate, OR\n- any `.scp/rule-config.yaml` entry on the SCP repo itself has\n  `disable: true` AND `expires_at < <UTC date>` (the SCP-self\n  half of TF-005 — adopter-side rule-config expiry is enforced at\n  PR time via SCP-E007, not here).\n\nThe release-gate also emits **warning** annotations\n(`SCP-EREL-001-warn`) on suspicious deprecation patterns\n(announced_release more than one major behind candidate) without\nblocking — operators triage manually.\n\n### Tag-cut procedure (operator)\n\nMandatory pre-flight + apply pattern. ALWAYS:\n\n1. **Author the release-prep PR.** Bump `version-manifest.json`;\n   add or remove entries in `policies/deprecations.yaml` per the\n   ramp; write release notes; merge to `main`.\n2. **Dry-run the gate.** `gh workflow run release-gate.yml -f dry_run_tag=<tag>` and wait for exit 0.\n3. **Push the tag.** Only after dry-run is clean. The post-tag\n   observer fires automatically as a final check.\n4. **Publish the GitHub release** + Renovate bump cascade per the\n   normal 020H part 2 procedure.\n\n### Bad-tag recovery procedure\n\nIf a tag is pushed that fails the post-tag observer:\n\n- **Do NOT attempt to delete or force-push the tag.** The D-030 +\n  D-034 tag-protection rulesets block deletion and force-push,\n  including for admins. The bad tag is immutable.\n- **Cut a corrected `v<X>.<Y+1>.0`** (next MINOR) that satisfies\n  the ramp. The bad tag remains in the tag list but is superseded\n  by the corrected one.\n- **Add a release note on the bad tag's GitHub release page**\n  documenting the violation + pointing adopters to the corrected\n  tag. Detection latency depends on the adopter's bump path:\n  - **Renovate-using adopters** (the §12.7.2 recommended path) see\n    the automated bump PR to `v<X>.<Y+1>.0` within hours of\n    publication; the bump PR is the primary signal.\n  - **Manually SHA-pinning adopters** see no immediate signal at\n    all. The `SCP-FRESH-001` freshness warning (ADOPT-001 §12.7.11)\n    fires only when the wrapper is more than `freshness_warning_threshold_minor` (default 2) MINOR releases behind main HEAD —\n    so an adopter pinned to the bad v<X>.<Y>.<Z> sees the warning\n    only after `v<X>.<Y+3>.0` has been cut. Manual quarterly review\n    of the SCP releases page (per the §12.7.11 manual fallback) is\n    the supplementary signal for this cohort.\n- **In an emergency only** (e.g. the bad tag introduced a security\n  vulnerability that publishing a corrected tag does not\n  immediately mitigate), the temporary-ruleset-disable path is:\n\n  ```bash\n  # 1. Discover the ruleset id.\n  gh api repos/jrnb2024/standards-control-plane/rulesets \\\n    --jq '.[] | {id, name}'\n\n  # 2. Delete the ruleset (requires administration:write PAT).\n  gh api -X DELETE repos/jrnb2024/standards-control-plane/rulesets/<id>\n\n  # 3. Delete the bad tag.\n  git push --delete origin v<X>.<Y>.<Z>\n\n  # 4. Restore the ruleset (idempotent; reproduces the D-030 state).\n  bash scripts/configure-020j-protections.sh\n  ```\n\n  This bypasses the bus-factor-1 protection and MUST be paired with\n  an amending decision row in `docs/DECISIONS.md` (closes 020H.3\n  R2 COR-nit-002).\n\nRule deprecation specifically: when an `SCP-R-NNN` rule is\ndeprecated:\n\n- The rule's deny continues to fire at its current `threshold:` value\n  during the deprecation window.\n- **The rule's own Rego implementation** emits a per-PR\n  `::warning::SCP-R-NNN deprecated; will be removed in v<X+1>.0.0; <migration-pointer>`\n  annotation. There is no centralized emitter — each rule self-announces.\n  This is the `SCP-DEP-001` annotation class (registered in ADOPT-001\n  §12.7.7); the deprecation-PR adds the warning emission alongside\n  the existing rule logic and adds the matching entry to\n  `policies/deprecations.yaml`.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'rg -n \"prior_restore_evidence_present|check_forward_mode_safety|allow_force_pushes|allow_deletions|NO_PRIOR_GREEN_CI|paginate|re-armed|REPO_ROOT|CAUTION|restore\" scripts/enable-required-check.sh tests/check_invocation_log/test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh policies/VERSIONING.md docs/DECISIONS.md docs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/restore-roundtrip-evidence-PLACEHOLDER.md STATUS.md'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'rg -n \"prior_restore_evidence_present|check_forward_mode_safety|allow_force_pushes|allow_deletions|NO_PRIOR_GREEN_CI|paginate|re-armed|REPO_ROOT|CAUTION|restore\" scripts/enable-required-check.sh tests/check_invocation_log/test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh policies/VERSIONING.md docs/DECISIONS.md docs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/restore-roundtrip-evidence-PLACEHOLDER.md STATUS.md'","aggregated_output":"docs/DECISIONS.md:3:**Last Updated:** 2026-05-10 (D-047 filed for WP-SCP-024 024B-extras; restore/break-glass/workflow wiring)\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:33:> 024B-core; the deferred 024B-extras surface carries the `--restore`\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:92:| D-044 | 2026-05-09 | Adopt the WP-SCP-024 slice 024B-core operational contracts for cascade scaffolding. Components: (1) `scripts/scaffold-downstream.sh` (`SCP-073-scaffolder` per WP-SCP-020 §11 follow-up + WP-SCP-021 follow-up `SCP-075-scaffolder-compose`) generates adopter-side artefacts mechanically - bootstrap-only (refuses `CI=true` / `GITHUB_ACTIONS=true` per D-035 symmetry); validates `--scp-sha` against SCP main HEAD lineage (warns if not main HEAD; refuses if non-existent); emits a TF-023E-002 warning for post-v1.2.0 SHAs while recommending the v1.0.0 pin; `--scp-sha` 40-char hex regex; `--default-branch` enum {main, master, develop}; `--scorecard-emit` enum; `--output-dir` writability + path-normalised system-path denylist (incl `/private/var/*` macOS canonicalisation); emits `MANIFEST.json` with SHA256 audit; arguments per plan-doc §5.3. Canonical adopter slugs are normalization aids only, not collision-resistant IDs, so cohort repo names must remain unique after canonicalization. (2) `templates/adopter-wrapper.yml.tmpl` is the canonical adopter wrapper shape per ADOPT-001 §12 with Renovate inline-comment marker `# renovate: datasource=github-tags depName=jrnb2024/standards-control-plane` enabling auto-bump per plan-doc invariant 8 Threshold A criterion; substitutions `{{DEFAULT_BRANCH}}`, `{{SCP_SHA}}`, `{{SCORECARD_EMIT}}`; least-privilege workflow-level permissions (`contents:read` + `statuses:write` only). (3) `scripts/check-invocation-log-entry.sh` CLI tool implements plan-doc invariant 2 cascade-status CI enforcement: 4 enforcement behaviours (fail-closed default for absent/unrecognised; `onboarded` -> log-entry-modified + target-match; `onboarded-operator-bump` -> log entry + `STATUS.md` `TF-024X-renovate-<slug>` row matching invariant 2 regex literally; `blocked-on-adopter-conflict` -> `DISPATCH-NOTE` `TF-024X-conflict-<adopter>` reference + log file NOT modified) + explicit tooling-slice opt-in gate for `cascade-status: not applicable` (`--allow-not-applicable`; default refusal for direct CLI use). Regex via `python3 re.search()` (PCRE-style); exactly-one-match assertions on both `cascade-status` and `**Target:**` extraction close multi-occurrence injection bypasses; adopter-slug canonicalisation per plan-doc spec. CLI tool only - GitHub Actions workflow wiring (`.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml`) defers to slice 024B-extras alongside `enable-required-check.sh --restore` mode + ADOPT-001 §12.8 break-glass procedure. D-044 was reserved for slice 024B at WP-SCP-024 plan-doc 024A merge (PR #102, 2026-05-04); after the operator-decided scope-split (SCOPE-CORRECTION-2026-05-09.md), D-044 stays scoped to core deliverables; sibling D-NNN may be reserved at 024B-extras authoring time for the deferred surface (`--restore` + break-glass + workflow wiring). Slice 024B-core ships under documented protocol deviation per feedback_four_tier_dispatch.md note + justify rule (kernel hook lives in ACC repo only; per-repo install pattern is FUP-ACC-INSTALL-TARGET-REPO-001 - open). | ACCEPTED | D-044 was reserved at WP-SCP-024 plan-doc 024A merge per the §9 reservation block. The original 024B accumulated 7 fix-rounds + 7 R-rounds against a single branch with each round closing 5-6 MAJ but introducing 2-3 new defects in just-added code (R6 missed primary-deliverable workflow wiring; R7 fix introduced bootstrap defect on slice's own PR). Empirical signal: surface area too large (16 files, ~3500 lines added) for single-pass convergence. Operator decided 2026-05-09 to split 024B into 024B-core (this slice; ~5 files; scaffolder + template + CI enforcement script + tests) + 024B-extras (deferred; `--restore` mode + ADOPT-001 §12.8 break-glass + `.github/workflows/` CI wiring + step 7 operator-interactive demo). Split is incremental delivery, NOT descope - both halves still ship; both required before 024C cohort onboarding opens. Original 024B work preserved at `feature/wp-scp-024-024b-extras-parking` branch (audit trail: 7 codex-fix-round-N-audit.log files + 7 R-round archive directories incl r8-archive carry-forward findings). Slice 024B-core scope is internally coherent: scaffolder generates adopter artefacts; CI enforcement script (CLI) validates cascade-status declarations; tests cover both. The CLI script can be invoked manually as a stop-gap until 024B-extras wires it into GitHub Actions. The CLI guard is necessary-but-not-sufficient: workflow-side hardcoding of `--tooling-slice-id` and omission of `--allow-not-applicable` in 024B-extras is the canonical closure path for the operator-supplied not-applicable bypass surface (see FUP-024B-CORE-NOT-APPLICABLE-WORKFLOW-001). Bus-factor-1 acknowledged (D-031); 2026-07-21 quarterly review covers. Identified at WP-SCP-024 plan-doc §9 D-044 reservation |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:93:| D-047 | 2026-05-10 | Adopt WP-SCP-024 024B-extras operational contracts: `scripts/enable-required-check.sh --restore <pre-state.json>` restores branch protection from the captured prior-state log entry by transforming GET-shape JSON into the PUT body, stripping envelope fields recursively, converting `enforce_admins.enabled` to a boolean, and replaying `required_signatures` through the dedicated sub-resource; restore-mode posture-degradation flags `--i-understand-restore-removes-admin-enforcement` and `--i-understand-restore-removes-required-checks` are mandatory when the target removes those protections; forward-mode now performs a path-pinned workflow lookup for `.github/workflows/policy-check-wrapper.yml`, queries workflow-runs without a branch filter, validates `--expected-wrapper-sha` against actual release tags via `gh api repos/jrnb2024/standards-control-plane/git/ref/tags/<tag>`, and treats the working-tree diff of `docs/reviews/WP-SCP-020/branch-protection-log.md` as part of prior-entry detection; the new CI workflow `.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml` wires the CLI gate into PR checks with `paths-ignore: docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024[AB]*/**`; ADOPT-001 gains §12.8 break-glass procedure and explicitly names the `--i-understand-no-gate-2-verification` escape hatch; STATUS.md and the DISPATCH-NOTE placeholder for the step-7 operator demo are updated in-slice. | ACCEPTED | The 024B split left the restore / break-glass / workflow-integration surface as the deferred half so the review load stayed bounded. This decision ratifies the operational contract that lets operators disable and re-enable the federation primitive safely without widening the adopter-facing API surface, while preserving the bootstrap guard that prevents tooling slices from self-blocking their own PRs. The release-tag SHA requirement is intentionally anchored to actual git tags, not arbitrary commits, so Gate 3 can re-arm against a concrete release artifact rather than against moving main-head. Bus-factor-1 acknowledged: the helper remains operator-run, the escape hatch is explicitly auditable, and the restore demo evidence is still an operator-interactive step outside Codex dispatch. Identified at WP-SCP-024 024B-extras authoring time. |\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:122:NO_PRIOR_GREEN_CI=0\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:150:  --restore PRE-STATE.json\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:159:  --i-understand-restore-removes-admin-enforcement\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:160:                           Confirm a restore target that removes admin\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:162:  --i-understand-restore-removes-required-checks\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:163:                           Confirm a restore target that removes required\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:196:    --restore)\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:197:      [ $# -lt 2 ] && { echo \"error: --restore requires a value\" >&2; usage; exit 2; }\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:205:    --i-understand-this-repo-has-no-prior-green-ci) NO_PRIOR_GREEN_CI=1; shift ;;\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:206:    --i-understand-restore-removes-admin-enforcement) ACK_RESTORE_ADMIN_REMOVAL=1; shift ;;\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:207:    --i-understand-restore-removes-required-checks) ACK_RESTORE_REQUIRED_CHECKS_REMOVAL=1; shift ;;\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:222:    echo \"error: --restore requires a pre-state JSON path\" >&2\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:226:    echo \"error: --restore cannot be combined with --plan\" >&2\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:230:    echo \"error: --restore cannot be combined with --no-enforce-admins\" >&2\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:234:    echo \"error: --restore cannot be combined with --i-understand-this-bypasses-the-gate\" >&2\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:238:    echo \"error: --restore cannot be combined with --expected-wrapper-sha\" >&2\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:241:  if [ \"$NO_PRIOR_GREEN_CI\" -eq 1 ]; then\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:242:    echo \"error: --restore cannot be combined with --i-understand-this-repo-has-no-prior-green-ci\" >&2\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:246:    echo \"error: --restore cannot be combined with --i-understand-no-gate-2-verification\" >&2\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:256:if [ \"$NO_PRIOR_GREEN_CI\" -eq 1 ] && [ -n \"$EXPECTED_WRAPPER_SHA\" ]; then\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:332:validate_restore_source_json() {\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:343:    print(f\"error: unable to parse restore pre-state JSON: {exc}\", file=sys.stderr)\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:347:    print(\"error: restore pre-state JSON must be an object\", file=sys.stderr)\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:358:        print(f\"error: restore pre-state JSON missing required key '{key}'\", file=sys.stderr)\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:361:        print(f\"error: restore pre-state JSON key '{key}' has unexpected type\", file=sys.stderr)\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:445:prior_restore_evidence_present() {\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:475:  tag_list_json=\"$(gh api --paginate \"repos/jrnb2024/standards-control-plane/git/refs/tags?per_page=100\")\"\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:491:check_forward_mode_safety() {\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:494:  if [ \"$NO_PRIOR_GREEN_CI\" -eq 1 ]; then\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:519:  if prior_restore_evidence_present \"docs/reviews/WP-SCP-020/branch-protection-log.md\" \"${REPO}@${BRANCH}\"; then\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:521:      echo \"error: prior --restore evidence detected for ${REPO}@${BRANCH}; --expected-wrapper-sha <release-tag-sha> is required\" >&2\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:522:      echo \"       pass --i-understand-no-gate-2-verification to bypass Gate 2 verification (audited via CAUTION log entry)\" >&2\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:530:      log \"CAUTION: Gate 2 verification bypassed via --i-understand-no-gate-2-verification; the gate is re-armed against the current wrapper SHA\"\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:531:    elif ! prior_restore_evidence_present \"docs/reviews/WP-SCP-020/branch-protection-log.md\" \"${REPO}@${BRANCH}\"; then\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:532:      echo \"error: --expected-wrapper-sha requires prior --restore evidence for 