y minimum so the second maintainer has time to review; the 48h CEILING for auto-defer remains so abandoned proposals are surfaced. Symmetric with D-033's \"operational reality must amend the spec when the spec encounters a constraint that wasn't anticipated\" pattern. Identified at WP-SCP-022 slice 020L post-R2 fixpoint by operator (`@jrnb2024`) when reviewing the merge-readiness of PR #89 |\n| D-041 | 2026-05-03 | Adopt the cross-repo scorecard data shape (`schemas/scorecard-emit.schema.json` v0.1) + opt-in adopter participation model per WP-SCP-023 023B (this PR). The schema defines aggregated per-rule counts (raw_findings, denies, waived, rule_config_disabled), waivers aggregate (active_count, by_rule_id, expiring_within_30d), rule-config aggregate (disabled_rules, expiring_within_30d), repo / ref / commit / scp_version / RFC3339 emitted_at, and a verdict (allow/deny/warn). The schema EXPLICITLY DOES NOT include waiver content (`reason`, `approved_by`, `waiver_id` strings) — invariant 2 of WP-SCP-023 plan-doc binds this. The reusable workflow gains a `scorecard-emit: bool` `workflow_call` input (default false) so existing adopters see no behaviour change; opt-in adopters set `with: scorecard-emit: true`. Schema versioning: MAJOR-pinned per `policies/VERSIONING.md` D-036 + WP-SCP-023 plan-doc §10 Q1 — aggregator drops emits with unknown `schema_version`. Verification: GitHub Actions Artifact Attestation (OIDC-based) via `actions/attest-build-provenance@v4.1.0` (SHA `a2bbfa25...`) at emit time; aggregator verifies via `gh attestation verify --signer-workflow` (per D-042 to be filed at slice 023C). v1.2.0 cut on this slice's merge per VERSIONING.md MINOR category | ACCEPTED | This is the first slice of WP-SCP-023's implementation chain (023A plan-doc landed at PR #97, commit `7075234`, 2026-05-03 R4 fixpoint). The data shape was specified at plan-doc level; this slice ratifies it as code surface. Default-false on the workflow input is the load-bearing safety propert