{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_22","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'rg -n \"TF-024B-STEP7-DEMO-001|TF-024B-REQCHECK-ENABLE-001|Tracked-forward items from 024B|24B\" STATUS.md'","aggregated_output":"3:**Last updated:** 2026-05-10 (WP-SCP-024 024B-extras dispatch finalised; restore/break-glass/workflow wiring)\n119:| 6 | #102 | **024A** | WP-SCP-024 plan-doc v0.1 — estate cascade. Defines adopter cohort `{pim, recommender, shopify-app, mapp-doc-agent, control-tower}` (per D-035) explicitly **FLA-independent** per operator direction; canary-first sequencing PIM → control-tower → mapp-doc-agent + recommender → shopify-app; per-adopter onboarding contract (adopter PR + SCP-side cascade slice + invocation log + post-bake observation window ≥1 calendar week + ≥1 Renovate bump cycle). Reserves D-044/D-045/D-046 for implementation slices 024B/024C/024G. Threshold A: ≥3 of 5 cohort adopters required-check live + ≥1 SCP minor version-bump propagated cleanly via Renovate + USER-GATE-E signed. Required-check cascade is primary deliverable; scorecard-emit opt-in is secondary follow-up gated on TF-023E-002 closure, and 024B-core now warns on post-v1.2.0 SHAs while keeping the v1.0.0 pin as the operational fallback until TF-023E-002 closes. **Cascade-status spec hardened over 9 review rounds** (32 unique MAJ + 1 CRIT closed across 8 fix-rounds — unprecedented; cause was the cascade-status / CI-enforcement clause being structurally cross-cutting): 3 close-states (`onboarded`, `onboarded-operator-bump`, `blocked-on-adopter-conflict`) × 4 CI behaviours (3 named + fail-closed default) × (positive evidence + machine-enforceable regex format spec + negative assertion). WP-SCP-024 is the natural successor to the 5-move MVCP — turns SCP's estate observability (WP-SCP-023) into action. Merged at `4dc3faa`. |\n123:**Operator decision (locked 2026-05-09):** the 6 D-035-aligned rules previously framed as gating CT Wave 1 entry on 2026-05-15 are **RETIRED under that deadline** — re-scoped under WP-SCP-025 (parked, post-WP-SCP-024 Threshold A). The retirement is conditional on a strategic reframe: SCP's near-term credibility depends on shipping 2-3 high-value domain rules that catch things review misses + measurable adopter consumption (≥3 cohort adopters running ≥2 SCP-R-005+ rules with ≥80% pass rate over ≥4-week observation window), not on forcing the 6 SDK-discipline rules through under deadline pressure when (a) CT D-035 Phase 5 already shipped 2026-05-07 without these rules as preconditions; (b) WP-SCP-024 cascade is operator-decided FLA-independent per 2026-05-03 §2 invariants row 4; (c) none of the 6 had been drafted with 6 days remaining; (d) parallel work on slice 024B (the actual cascade gate per plan-doc §6) would have been diluted.\n137:**Slice 024B-core remains the immediate work** — hard predecessor for cohort onboarding 024C-F per WP-SCP-024 plan-doc §6. Scope: scaffolder + adopter wrapper template + `check-invocation-log-entry.sh` + tests; 024B-extras deferred.\n139:## Today's chain (2026-05-09 PM — slice 024B-core + scope-split decision)\n141:**Operator decision (locked 2026-05-09):** WP-SCP-024 slice 024B split into 024B-core (scaffolder + adopter wrapper template + cascade-status CI enforcement script + tests) + 024B-extras (`--restore` mode + ADOPT-001 §12.8 break-glass + `.github/workflows/` CI wiring + step 7 operator-interactive demo). Empirical justification: original 024B accumulated 7 fix-rounds + 7 R-rounds with each round closing 5-6 MAJ but introducing 2-3 new defects in just-added code; R6 missed a primary deliverable; R7 fix introduced bootstrap defect on slice's own PR. Surface-area-too-large for single-pass convergence. Split is incremental delivery, NOT descope — both halves still ship; both required before 024C cohort onboarding opens.\n143:Original 024B work preserved at branch `feature/wp-scp-024-024b-extras-parking` (pushed to origin 2026-05-09; audit trail intact: 7 codex-fix-round-N-audit.log + 7 R-round archive dirs).\n147:| 1 | Slice 024B-core: `scripts/scaffold-downstream.sh` + `templates/adopter-wrapper.yml.tmpl` + `scripts/check-invocation-log-entry.sh` (CLI) + `tests/scaffolder/test_scaffold_downstream.sh` + `tests/check_invocation_log/test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh` (cascade-status enforcement only). D-044 filed scoped to core. Branch: `feature/wp-scp-024-024b-core`. |\n148:| 2 | Slice 024B-extras: deferred. Scope: `enable-required-check.sh --restore` mode + ADOPT-001 §12.8 break-glass + `.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml` + step 7 operator-interactive `--restore` round-trip demo. To be branched from merged 024B-core. R8-CORR-001/002/003 (extras-parking r8-archive) carry forward as known findings. |\n149:| 3 | Plan-doc §6 amendment: 024C entry now conditional on BOTH 024B-core + 024B-extras merged + FUP-ACC-INSTALL-TARGET-REPO-001 closure (was: 024B + FUP-ACC-INSTALL-TARGET-REPO-001 closure). Cohort cascade gate unchanged in posture; precondition list extended for clarity. |\n151:## Today's chain (2026-05-10 — slice 024B-extras)\n155:| 1 | Slice 024B-extras: `scripts/enable-required-check.sh --restore` added with GET-shape → PUT-shape transform, posture-degradation acknowledgements, required-signatures sub-resource handling, and forward-mode safety checks (path-pinned workflow lookup, no branch filter on runs API, release-tag SHA validation, working-tree prior-entry detection). |\n158:| 4 | Step-7 operator-interactive demo evidence is still operator-run; placeholder path recorded at `docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/restore-roundtrip-evidence-PLACEHOLDER.md`; `feature/wp-scp-024-024b-extras-parking` may be deleted once both 024B-core and 024B-extras merge. |\n184:- ~~**TF-024B-core-WORKFLOW-MITIGATION-001**: 024B-extras workflow wiring will hardcode `--tooling-slice-id` per workflow file and omit `--allow-not-applicable` from cohort workflows, closing the residual operator-supplied slice-id bypass surface. 024B-core keeps the CLI guard + documentation only.~~ ✅ **closed in 024B-extras** via `.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml`; the workflow now hardcodes cohort precedence and fails closed on branch-protection-log edits that lack a cascade-slice DISPATCH-NOTE update.\n285:- **D-047 (2026-05-10)** — Adopt the WP-SCP-024 024B-extras restore / break-glass / workflow wiring defense, including the workflow-body cohort-precedence short-circuit and the invocation-log enforcement guard for branch-protection-log edits. This closes the workflow-side mitigation originally parked under TF-024B-core-WORKFLOW-MITIGATION-001.\n307:## Tracked-forward items from WP-SCP-024 024B-core / 024B-extras\n310:- **FUP-024B-CORE-NOT-APPLICABLE-WORKFLOW-001** (closed in fix-round-4; this commit): 024B-extras workflow wiring now skips script invocation entirely for tooling slices, so the residual operator-supplied `not applicable` bypass surface is gone without passing `--allow-not-applicable` or `--tooling-slice-id` into the script. Cohort cascade slices still invoke the script with full enforcement; defense-in-depth now comes from the workflow short-circuit plus the script's default refusal of `--allow-not-applicable`.\n311:- **TF-024B-STEP7-DEMO-001** (open): --restore real-repo round-trip evidence (docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/restore-roundtrip-evidence-PLACEHOLDER.md) — operator-interactive demo at dispatch-plan step 7; merge-blocking AC for 024B-extras per plan-doc §6 + 024A R1 MAJ-SAFE-003; closes when operator runs forward-mode + --restore round-trip on throw-away test repo + commits byte-for-byte match evidence.\n312:- **TF-024B-SCAFFOLDER-023E002-UPDATE** (open): when TF-023E-002 closes, remove the post-v1.2.0 warning block from `scripts/scaffold-downstream.sh` and delete the cutover ancestry guard that keeps the v1.0.0 fallback recommendation alive. The scaffolder should stop warning only after the separate `attest-scorecard` workflow restructuring lands. Owner: @jrnb2024.\n"